From f9601e6cfefc77a1589db1979eb97b6fdb59db33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nebur692 <nebur_692@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:59:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tests: GHSA-r6x9-5r99-36j7 stmt-response-field-len-premature,
 upstream's check order

This source checks that the fixed-length field metadata (length byte plus
12 bytes) is in the packet BEFORE testing the length byte, as upstream 8.x
does (BAIL_IF_NOT_ENOUGH_DATA_EX(1 + 2 + 4 + 1 + 2 + 1 + 2)). Our test was
written for the older order (7.3/7.4), where the "Protocol error. Server
sent false length. Expected 12" warning comes first. The packet is still
rejected with "Premature end of data" and nothing is read past the
buffer; only that warning is gone, so the expectation drops it.
---
 .../ghsa-r6x9-5r99-36j7-stmt-response-field-len-premature.phpt  | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/mysqli/tests/ghsa-r6x9-5r99-36j7-stmt-response-field-len-premature.phpt b/ext/mysqli/tests/ghsa-r6x9-5r99-36j7-stmt-response-field-len-premature.phpt
index 59e2cb80..42c03b0d 100644
--- a/ext/mysqli/tests/ghsa-r6x9-5r99-36j7-stmt-response-field-len-premature.phpt
+++ b/ext/mysqli/tests/ghsa-r6x9-5r99-36j7-stmt-response-field-len-premature.phpt
@@ -34,8 +34,6 @@ print "done!";
 [*] Received: 170000001653454c454354206974656d2046524f4d206974656d73
 [*] Sending - Malicious Stmt Prepare items [Field length over-read]: 0c0000010001000000010000000000003000000203646566087068705f74657374056974656d73056974656d73046974656d0c6974656d0ce000c8000000fd011000000005000003fe00000200
 
-Warning: mysqli::prepare(): Protocol error. Server sent false length. Expected 12 in %s on line %d
-
 Warning: mysqli::prepare(): Premature end of data (mysqlnd_wireprotocol.c:%d) in %s on line %d
 
 Warning: mysqli::prepare(): Result set field packet shorter than expected in %s on line %d
-- 
2.55.0

